# Super-Adaptoid's power is defined by a characteristic-defining ability (CR 604.3): once Abigale, Eloquent First-Year's
# trigger makes it lose all abilities, nothing defines its power and its * is 0 (CR 208.2a, 613.1f), so it is a 0/2 - though
# Bot1 controls two legendary creatures - with the flying, first strike and lifelink of the counters put on it afterwards.
# Turn 1: Mox Pearl and Mox Jet pay Super-Adaptoid (its trigger has no other creature to target). Turn 3: Swamp and Plains pay
# Abigale, whose trigger targets Super-Adaptoid.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Pearl
Mox Jet
Super-Adaptoid
Swamp
Plains
Abigale, Eloquent First-Year
Island x14

[Bot2 Deck]
Island x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Swamp.Play
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Super-Adaptoid.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
? Bot1.Battlefield.Super-Adaptoid.Power = 1
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Plains.Play
Bot1.Battlefield.Swamp.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Plains.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Abigale, Eloquent First-Year.Cast
Bot1.Target(Super-Adaptoid)
[T3 Bot1.Main2]

[Expect]
Bot1.Battlefield.Super-Adaptoid.Power = 0
Bot1.Battlefield.Super-Adaptoid.Toughness = 2
Bot1.Battlefield.Super-Adaptoid.Keywords = FirstStrike; Flying; Lifelink
Bot1.Battlefield.Abigale, Eloquent First-Year.Keywords = FirstStrike; Flying; Lifelink
